WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[MUSIC]

00:00:11.384 --> 00:00:14.073
The work I've done over the last 30

00:00:14.073 --> 00:00:16.501
years since I left the GSB has been

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:19.020
very interesting intersection of

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.104
business and technology and

00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:22.168
creativity.

00:00:22.168 --> 00:00:24.484
It's only after I left the business

00:00:24.484 --> 00:00:26.723
school that I came to enjoy working

00:00:26.723 --> 00:00:28.035
with technology and

00:00:28.035 --> 00:00:29.820
doing cool things with it.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.001
When I graduated, there was a huge

00:00:34.001 --> 00:00:35.446
recession and I kind of decided to

00:00:35.446 --> 00:00:37.420
go the entrepreneurial route.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.602
Did when startup

00:00:38.602 --> 00:00:40.375
doing control systems or

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:42.914
focus was on doing large concerts.

00:00:42.914 --> 00:00:45.525
We had clients the Grateful Dead

00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:46.497
actually.

00:00:46.497 --> 00:00:48.524
So I graduated from Stanford and

00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:50.399
a year later I was on tour with a

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:52.662
Grateful Dead living in a tour bus.

00:00:52.662 --> 00:00:54.384
It really helped me learn how

00:00:54.384 --> 00:00:56.394
the product work how the industry

00:00:56.394 --> 00:00:58.331
works, learn the customers and

00:00:58.331 --> 00:01:00.412
it was incredibly educational for

00:01:00.412 --> 00:01:02.278
my six weeks of concert touring

00:01:02.278 --> 00:01:03.680
being a roadie.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.408
We sold that company and then saw

00:01:05.408 --> 00:01:06.880
that video that I was really

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.864
inspired by these professors flying

00:01:08.864 --> 00:01:10.784
fleets of drones, information and

00:01:10.784 --> 00:01:12.576
then I thought, wow, that'd be

00:01:12.576 --> 00:01:14.650
really cool to do an entertainment.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.758
So I found a group of

00:01:15.758 --> 00:01:17.492
young robotics engineers and

00:01:17.492 --> 00:01:19.432
we joined forces, we spent three

00:01:19.432 --> 00:01:21.583
years developing the technology and

00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:23.385
then have been flying shows for

00:01:23.385 --> 00:01:24.580
the last two years.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.846
We make drones and the software

00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:29.722
needed to have them all perform

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.813
in a coordinated manner, to do all

00:01:31.813 --> 00:01:33.990
the interesting things in the sky.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.989
Drones can make almost anything

00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:37.659
in the sky,

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:40.070
they are 3D repositionable pixels.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.188
And so we are developing an entire

00:01:42.188 --> 00:01:44.532
system, both hardware and software

00:01:44.532 --> 00:01:46.648
that makes it easy to deploy these

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:48.084
drones and have them do

00:01:48.084 --> 00:01:50.220
what our clients want them to do.

00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:57.455
So entrepreneurial courses

00:01:57.455 --> 00:01:59.346
at Stanford gave me a really solid

00:01:59.346 --> 00:02:01.237
grounding in terms of how to think

00:02:01.237 --> 00:02:03.138
about business opportunities.

00:02:03.138 --> 00:02:05.142
What's needed to get in place in

00:02:05.142 --> 00:02:06.775
order to be successful how

00:02:06.775 --> 00:02:08.259
to think long term how to

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:09.758
think strategically.

00:02:09.758 --> 00:02:11.824
Many of these lessons hold true

00:02:11.824 --> 00:02:14.049
today and are really important as

00:02:14.049 --> 00:02:16.194
you're figuring out how to grow

00:02:16.194 --> 00:02:18.420
a business into something really

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.181
successful and lasting.

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:22.076
Where things have shifted for

00:02:22.076 --> 00:02:24.197
me lately is normally I was behind

00:02:24.197 --> 00:02:25.042
the scenes.

00:02:25.042 --> 00:02:26.834
And because we are exploring new

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.294
territory with drones and

00:02:28.294 --> 00:02:30.152
pushing the envelope we've been

00:02:30.152 --> 00:02:32.221
much more the creatives ourselves.

00:02:32.221 --> 00:02:33.675
That's why we just went

00:02:33.675 --> 00:02:35.782
on America's Got Talent and it was

00:02:35.782 --> 00:02:37.899
a really kind of crazy situation.

00:02:37.899 --> 00:02:40.311
Because I never really envisioned

00:02:40.311 --> 00:02:42.057
myself being on stage but

00:02:42.057 --> 00:02:44.133
there I was, and we put on this

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.303
really awesome performance.

00:02:46.303 --> 00:02:47.916
And it was different and

00:02:47.916 --> 00:02:50.091
unusual to actually sort of be in

00:02:50.091 --> 00:02:51.623
front of the camera and

00:02:51.623 --> 00:02:53.880
be the talent and to be showcasing

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.297
the work that we've been working so

00:02:56.297 --> 00:02:58.567
hard on over the last five years.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.800
[MUSIC]

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.056
So one of the things that they

00:03:03.056 --> 00:03:05.594
always talked about at Stanford

00:03:05.594 --> 00:03:08.133
during In the entrepreneurship

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.765
classes is that there is no single

00:03:10.765 --> 00:03:11.337
path.

00:03:11.337 --> 00:03:13.851
And that entrepreneurs come from

00:03:13.851 --> 00:03:15.376
all walks of life and

00:03:15.376 --> 00:03:18.160
there are opportunities everywhere

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.131
and I think I have lived that 100%.

00:03:21.131 --> 00:03:23.828
My name is Nils Thorjussen I'm

00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:25.805
the CEO of Verge Aero.

